# Production Environment Variables for RF-FALCON-IDS

# Backend canister ID (REQUIRED for IC deployment, OPTIONAL for static hosting)
# 
# For IC Deployment (build-time injection):
#   This must be set BEFORE building the frontend:
#     export VITE_BACKEND_CANISTER_ID=$(dfx canister id backend --network ic)
#     pnpm run build
#   The build process validates this format and will fail with clear errors if invalid
# 
# For Static Hosting (runtime configuration):
#   Leave this empty during build
#   After deployment, edit /runtime-config.json in your deployed site to set the backend canister ID
#   This allows configuration without rebuilding
# 
# Format: xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-xxx (IC principal format)
VITE_BACKEND_CANISTER_ID=

# Internet Identity URL (production)
VITE_II_URL=https://identity.ic0.app

# Optional: Internet Identity derivation origin
# Only needed if using alternative domains
# VITE_II_DERIVATION_ORIGIN=

# Optional: CDN base URL for static assets
# Leave empty to serve assets from IC canister (default)
# Set to CDN origin to enable CDN delivery
# Example: VITE_ASSET_BASE_URL=https://cdn.example.com
VITE_ASSET_BASE_URL=

# CRITICAL NOTES:
# 
# IC Deployment:
#   - VITE_BACKEND_CANISTER_ID is injected at BUILD TIME, not runtime
#   - The build will fail immediately if this value is present but invalid
#   - The deployment script (scripts/deploy-mainnet.sh) handles this automatically
#   - Manual builds require: export VITE_BACKEND_CANISTER_ID=<canister-id>
# 
# Static Hosting:
#   - Build without VITE_BACKEND_CANISTER_ID (or leave empty)
#   - After deployment, edit /runtime-config.json in your deployed site
#   - Set backendCanisterId to your backend canister principal ID
#   - Reload the page to apply the configuration
# 
# Do not commit actual canister IDs to version control
# See DEPLOYMENT.md for detailed deployment instructions
